        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="notes" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;" value="&lt;b&gt;Draft 2026-11-11&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Sources: DAQ VD Fiber Plant v3; &amp;quot;VD onDetector Rack View of Cabling&amp;quot; (TMS, stamped 16SEPT2026); &amp;quot;VD Cryostat 27U Detector Racks&amp;quot; naming drawing (20 N + 20 S racks); &amp;quot;DAQ Readout Network&amp;quot; PRR specification (EDMS 3463072, v1.0, 21 May 2026).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Open items&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;1. Purchase ownership assumed by analogy with TDE and PDS, not confirmed: BDE buys the WIEC electronics, the MTP12 pigtails to the 27U patch panel, the RJ45 Cu cables and the timing fibers from the PTCs to the splitter; racks and the patch cord from the 1G switch to the 27U patch panel are FDC I&amp;amp;I.&lt;br&gt;2. The patching between the trunk patch panel and the readout switches (top-of-rack patch panels, MTP-12 into 4-way breakout transceivers, per EDMS 3463072) is not drawn in detail.&lt;br&gt;3. DTS fanout rack on the cryostat roof: rack name and location, fanout hardware, number of fibers from the DTS master and its Ctrl network connection are not defined here.&lt;br&gt;4. The 1G ports for the CRP level meter and the DPS PDU on the TMS sheet (&amp;quot;2x1G DPS&amp;quot; in the VD overview) are not drawn here.&lt;br&gt;5. Two 10G Ctrl uplinks per 27U rack are assumed.&lt;br&gt;6. Follow-up: who purchases the 2xLC patch cord from the DAQ barracks patch panel to the Ctrl network switch (drawn as DAQ)." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="740" y="1170" width="1330" height="355" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
